menu "HiYaKa PCA diagnostic safety"

config HI_YAKA_PCA_STRAPS_FIXED
    bool "Confirm PN532 mode straps are physically fixed before any I2C trial"
    default n
    help
        The c0 sample previously had R73/R74 removed and floating PN532 mode
        inputs. Leave this disabled until the physical strap state is fixed
        and recorded. The default image only logs HOLD and performs no bus
        transaction.

config HI_YAKA_PCA_ALLOW_FLOATING_PN532_CONFOUNDER
    bool "Allow the recorded c0 floating-PN532 state as a confounded A/B trial"
    default n
    help
        This does not claim the PN532 straps are valid. It only permits the
        hardware-versus-software I2C ABBA experiment on the already recorded
        c0 sample whose R73/R74 are removed. Results must be labelled
        PN532_FLOATING_CONFOUNDED and cannot close the shared-bus root cause.

endmenu
